d 'KSTEST': module to perform a k-sample Kolmogorov-Smirnov equality-of-distributions test
d
d  kstest performs a (optionally weighted) k-sample
d Kolmogorov-Smirnov (KS) permutation test to assess whether k >= 2
d samples come from the same distribution, as proposed by Kiefer
d (1959). It is the k-sample generalization of the two-sample test
d (Kolmogorov 1933; Smirnov 1948).  When k > 2, there is no single
d pairwise comparison to make, so kstest instead compares each
d group's empirical CDF to the (weighted) pooled empirical CDF of
d all groups combined and combines the discrepancies into a single
d statistic based on the T statistic of Kiefer (1959). 
d
d KW: equality of distributions
d KW: k-sample
d KW: Kolmogorov-Smirnov
d KW: comparisons
d KW: weighting
d
d Requires: Stata version 11
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260805
d
d Author: Ariel Linden, Linden Consulting Group, LLC
d Support: email alinden@@lindenconsulting.org
d
f kstest.ado
f kstest.sthlp
